<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116502" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤψ</span></b> , ἡ, <i><span class="en">
			<u>EM</u>
			344.55
		</span></i>, but ὁ, <i><span class="en">
			Ar.Byz.
		</span></i> (v. infr.), <i><span class="en">
			Eust.
			1426.55
		</span></i> (v. infr.), gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠπός,</span> acc.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦπα</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>eye, face, countenance,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
			</span></i>, only in acc. sing.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ὦπα
				ἰδέσθαι τινί</span> to look one in <i>the face,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.373
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὴν ἔλθητε Διός τ᾽ εἰς ὦπα
					ἴδησθε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					15.147
				</span></i>
			: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεινὸς εἰς ὦπα ἰδέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					22.405
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				23.107
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῇς εἰς ὦπα ἔοικεν</span>
			in <i>face</i> she is like the goddesses, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.158
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ μὲν γάρ τι κακῷ εἰς ὦπα ἐῴκει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.411
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῇς εἰς ὦπα ἐΐσκειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					62
				</span></i>
			.—masc. acc. pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεγάλους ὦπας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
				</span></i>
			 Byz. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				7.287b
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				9.367a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.804
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
			</span></i> l. c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διγλήνους ὦπας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					6.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				233.32
			</span></i>: but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ὦπα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Cra.</u>
					409c
				</span></i>
			: dat. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤπεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Max.
					157
				</span></i>
			. (Cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
				</span></i>
			)</div>
